    "question": {
      ":question/id": "df205313-5532-5f33-9fe7-0e8816c9b2de",
      ":question/problem": "![](generate/scratch/17592186059715-draft/plots/3fba3c297362c77d86a993b8.png)\n\nLet $A(0, 1)$ and $B(6, 6)$. Find $|\\overset{\\to }{AB}|$.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{OA}=a=j, \\\\ & \\overset{\\to }{OB}=b=6i+6j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} &= \\overset{\\to }{OB}-\\overset{\\to }{OA} \\\\ &= b-a \\\\ &= (6i+6j)-(j) \\\\ &= 6i+5j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe displacement components are $(6)-(0)=6$ and $(6)-(1)=5$.\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\overset{\\to }{AB}| &= \\sqrt{(6)^{2}+(5)^{2}} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{36+25} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{61}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
