    "question": {
      ":question/id": "2386b935-0034-5fc9-b9d0-a10244ce8479",
      ":question/problem": "![](generate/scratch/17592186059715-draft/plots/dd4fec8867232251ac034e4f.png)\n\nLet $C(-5,-5)$ and $D(3,2).$ Find $|\\overset{\\to }{CD}|.$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{OC}=c=-5i-5j, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{OD}=d=3i+2j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overset{\\to }{CD}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{CD} & =\\overset{\\to }{OD}-\\overset{\\to }{OC} \\\\  & =d-c \\\\  & =(3i+2j)-(-5i-5j) \\\\  & =8i+7j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe displacement components are $(3)-(-5)=8$ and $(2)-(-5)=7$.\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\overset{\\to }{CD}| & =\\sqrt{{8}^{2}+(7)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{64+49} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{113}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
