    "question": {
      ":question/id": "5876fc63-0c74-5829-ad3a-d7e7b76e5838",
      ":question/problem": "![](generate/scratch/17592186059715-draft/plots/aa5f241d606023b5ab8ca805.png)\n\nPoints $P$ and $Q$ are shown in the picture above. Find $|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}|$.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/worked-solution": "From the picture, we obtain $P(-8,8)$ and $Q(4,-3).$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{OP}=p=-8i+8j, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{OQ}=q=4i-3j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =q-p \\\\  & =(4i-3j)-(-8i+8j) \\\\  & =12i-11j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe displacement components are $(4)-(-8)=12$ and $(-3)-(8)=-11$.\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| & =\\sqrt{{12}^{2}+(-11)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{144+121} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{265}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
